# `{ check: kind, ...normalize(params), least }`: what is spread is anything, so the checked type of the literal lists nothing; the literal listed nothing either, and Link appended `check` and `least` out of line.
# Now it lists the names that it writes itself. What a spread between them must keep: the order of keys . who lays anew . indices . getters read once . what is not enumerable . an own __proto__ . symbols . the order of evaluation. As plain.
